# More info: https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#dockerignore-file
#
# This is a DENY list, not an allow list, and deliberately so.
#
# The previous version denied everything with "**" and re-included sources with
# "!**/*.go". BuildKit honours that; Buildah does not expand "**/*.ext"
# re-includes the same way, so under podman the build context arrived with no
# Go files at all and the image build failed with "package cmd/... is not in
# std". Listing what to exclude behaves identically across both builders.
#
# Keep this list conservative: an entry that wrongly excludes a source file
# breaks the build loudly, but one that wrongly includes a directory only makes
# the context bigger.

# Version control and CI definitions.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# Build outputs and downloaded tooling.
bin/
dist/

# Test-only assets that the images never run.
test/

# The raw model downloads. Only the CONVERTED artifacts next to them
# (potion/model.bin, potion/vocab.txt, minilm/model.onnx, minilm/vocab.txt)
# are baked into the images; the safetensors and tokenizer.json they were
# derived from would add well over 100 MiB for nothing.
hack/models/.cache/

# Documentation and packaging metadata.
docs/
*.md
LICENSE
PROJECT

# Container and build definitions -- copying these into the image would
# invalidate its cache on every Dockerfile edit.
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.*
Makefile
.dockerignore

# Local editor and tool artifacts.
*.code-workspace
.idea/
.vscode/
graphify-out/

# Go test binaries and coverage output.
*.test
*.out
